Check assignment, sample-ratio mismatch, exposure and eligibility, duplicate users, contamination, missingness, and duration. Define the estimand, absolute/relative effects, intervals, and test. Explain multiplicity or peeking. Do not rely on a p-value alone or claim causality before validating assumptions.

