Match the task to trend, comparison, distribution, relationship, composition, or geography. Recommend a primary and alternate chart; define axes, units, sorting, grouping, colors, baseline, uncertainty, and annotations. Avoid misleading dual axes, exaggerated truncated scales, excessive series, and unnecessary 3D.

